# NaukriBoost — B2C SaaS Implementation Plan

## Vision
A web application where users sign up, connect their Naukri account (one-time browser login), upload their resume, and the system automatically keeps their profile "fresh" daily — boosting visibility to recruiters. Users get a dashboard to track all activity.

---

## GDPR Explainer (Your Question)

**GDPR** (General Data Protection Regulation) is a European Union law, but its principles apply globally as a best practice when you're storing personal user data. Here's why it matters for us:

| Concern | What It Means for NaukriBoost | How We Handle It |
|---|---|---|
| **Storing passwords** | If we store a user's Naukri password and get hacked, their Naukri account is compromised | **We DON'T store passwords.** We use session-capture — user logs in once in a browser, we save the session cookies only |
| **Personal data** | Resume files contain name, phone, address, education — highly sensitive | Encrypt resumes at rest, auto-delete after upload, let users delete anytime |
| **Right to deletion** | Users must be able to delete ALL their data from our system | Provide a "Delete My Account" button that wipes everything |
| **Consent** | Users must explicitly agree to what we do with their data | Clear Terms of Service + Privacy Policy at signup |
| **Data breach notification** | If hacked, we must inform affected users | Good security practices to prevent this |

> [!TIP]
> **Our approach eliminates the biggest GDPR risk**: We never store Naukri passwords. The session-capture model means we only hold browser cookies that expire naturally. This is much safer than storing credentials.

