## Session Capture Flow (Critical Path)

This is how we connect a user's Naukri account without storing their password:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Frontend
    participant Backend
    participant Browser as Stealth Browser

    User->>Frontend: Clicks "Connect Naukri"
    Frontend->>Backend: POST /api/naukri/connect
    Backend->>Browser: Launch headed Playwright (stealth)
    Browser->>Browser: Navigate to naukri.com/nlogin/login
    Note over Browser: User sees real Naukri login page
    User->>Browser: Enters email + password manually
    Browser->>Browser: Naukri authenticates
    Browser->>Backend: Capture storageState (cookies)
    Backend->>Backend: Encrypt & save to naukri_sessions
    Backend->>Frontend: { status: "connected" }
    Frontend->>User: "✅ Naukri Connected!"
```

> [!NOTE]
> On the local machine, this opens a real browser window. When we move to cloud, this becomes a remote browser session (via noVNC or a similar approach) streamed to the user's browser — that's a Phase 2 concern.

